Instructions for compiling and executing C# code on Linux.

C# language uses Just-In-Time (JIT) compiler development similar to Java.
You can compile on Linux and execute under Windows (if you have .net) and 
under Linux using mono.

Compile a C# source into an executable named filename.exe

  $ mcs {filename.cs}

Execute the C# application  

  $ mono {filename.exe}

Debug your executable:

  $ mcs -debug {filename.exe}
  $ mdb {filename.exe}
